WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.230
Good morning John; it's Friday, April 22nd.

00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:06.130
So, I made a video for today, uh, and it's
all ready, it's all edited, it's ready to

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.780
go. Due to circumstances beyond my control,
which I cannot explain to you at this very

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.539
moment, I cannot put that video online.

00:00:11.539 --> 00:00:16.910
So now, I have to make another video. Gyeahh.
So since my planned video for today kind of

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.290
fell through, now I have to make a video in
the old school way. The way that I used to

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.519
do it where I just, uh, talk to the camera--
hi!

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:26.029
This is a prop for the video that was supposed
to go online today - it's a hundred pennies

00:00:26.029 --> 00:00:30.300
in a cup. And this is a prop from my nerd
jokes video - it was around the lens. I don't

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.930
actually keep my duct tape there. Maybe I
should - uh, it's a place to keep it! Less

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:34.930
clutter.

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:37.870
Speaking of props, astute Nerdfighters who
watch every one of my videos - thank you very

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.219
much for doing that - have recently noticed
that my posters, uh, the one that's right

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:44.260
there, seems to keep changing. And that is
correct, I've been doing that for a while

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.690
now, where I rotate through posters because
I feel like, you know that's a space that

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.260
I can do interesting stuff with. And that
is the map of the Realm of Narnia.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:54.350
Speaking of good Nerdfighters who I appreciate
greatly, if you've been around since the rap

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:58.579
of the melm of-- rap of the melm. If you've
been around since the map of the Realm of

00:00:58.579 --> 00:01:00.140
Narnia days, uh, I am amazed.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.789
If you don't know what I'm talking about...

00:01:01.789 --> 00:01:07.600
"I love... that, right there, you see it?
That's a map of the Realm of Narnia."

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.610
Good Lord. I just went and watched that whole
video. That was January 5th, that was like

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.360
my, my third video ever on YouTube. Wow.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:21.890
And that, uh, co-starred with me! I recently
discovered, it was made in 1972! It's very-

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:27.270
it's pretty old! And so I went online... that
thing sells on eBay for like 80 to 100 dollars.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:30.530
And it's not like I haven't been fond of the
map of the Realm of Narnia, but knowing that

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:34.280
it's worth 80 bucks, bound to be a little
more careful with it in the future.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.360
So anyways, posters, I've decided that I want
more posters in my life, so I'm going to do

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.729
a rotation. Every video, new poster there.
And the first comment that tells me what that

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:46.219
poster is of, uh, you will get... nothing.

00:01:46.219 --> 00:01:49.920
DFTBA Records has not, to this point, done
posters, but I am obviously a fan of posters.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.950
So I want to do posters, but we need some
good poster designs. So I'm going to be looking

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.909
into that. Ideas for good poster designs in
the comments please.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:00.890
I have a tiny The Cheat, also I got him along
with my Strong Bad poster-- why is my chair

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:03.110
doing this?

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:08.560
[sped up talking]

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.700
Finally stopped. I'm dizzy. I should show
you, my feet aren't touching the ground. Leg-crossing

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.800
is one of my only stupid human tricks. I can
get into a full lotus without- without touching

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.720
my hands. And now you've seen my feet. Uh,
they're big, and not very attractive. Hiii!

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.820
John, we've been doing this for a long time;
when I went back to check out the Narnia video,

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:29.800
it really sort of hit home. Also, the amount
of amazing stuff that has happened to us.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.100
And that we have been able to accomplish because
of this.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.660
This, for example, like this is not something
that I could've done without - why did my

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:41.050
door just open? If I had had this idea, and
I didn't have Nerdfighteria to sort of as

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.680
a launching platform for it, I couldn't have
done anything with it. Nerdfighteria is there

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.510
to support me and the hare-brained schemes
that I have.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:52.780
And it's everything from that to, like, me
humping stuff on Tumblr - yes, I know I didn't

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:56.970
mention it in my last video, but don't worry,
I was impressed. And then you have more serious

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:00.440
stuff, like the Project For Awesome and the
fact that I was able to go to Haiti to examine

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.190
the work that non-profit organizations are
doing there.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:06.870
I sit here in this chair and I make videos
- I can't express how thankful I am for that,

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:10.840
and this probably should be, like, the video
that I make when we get 500,000 subscribers,

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:15.230
when I'm like "oh, thank you all," but I don't
need a special occasion. So somehow, this

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:19.000
video turned into a thank you video. I would
also like to thank ticky-tacky, for helping

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.830
to affix my posters to the walls. Uh, 3M is
not sponsoring this video.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:24.470
You may have noticed, we don't do much in
the way of sponsored videos. Why do I need

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.820
to do sponsored videos when I have my own
things to sell? Speaking of my own things

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:31.041
to sell, these are available on Amazon, I-
I know not everybody has a Paypal account

00:03:31.041 --> 00:03:33.360
or wants a Paypal account, so now you can
buy them on Amazon.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.540
Portal 2 is going well, I just uploaded the
second episode, uh, sorry it took me so long

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.360
to get it online, but MAN IS IT FUN!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.030
John, thank you as well; I hope you're having
a great time in Amsterdam, and I will see

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.030
you on Monday.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:48.180
End screen time! I just wanted to show you
this picture I just found of John Green, uh,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:54.010
this was when I was in college, so he was
just out of college, and this is my dorm room

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:58.840
in college. We had a dartboard - that is the
dart, John is throwing it - and he's super

00:03:58.840 --> 00:03:59.580
freakin' skinny!

